1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:27,900
Leo's Runner-Up title is legit.

3
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:29,340
The hardest thing to endure in life is...

4
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:30,780
when the shower water pressure is this weak.

5
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:32,190
Shawn!

6
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:35,100
You cannot tell anyone about this.

7
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:36,720
Don't tell a single soul, got it?

8
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:37,500
Ah!

9
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:39,900
Shawn, what are you doing?!

10
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:41,820
I'm absorbing the essence of the Earth!

11
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:44,220
Leo's gonna get kicked off the Team sooner or later.

12
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:47,100
Sticking with Mark is your only way out.

13
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,540
What's it to you?

14
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,940
Speed isn't absolute.

15
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:52,860
It's relative.

16
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,900
Episode 7

17
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,820
Whoa, Chuck's actually killing it!

18
00:02:06,280 --> 00:02:07,260
No way.

19
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:10,140
How is Chuck this good?

20
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:11,580
There's gotta be a trick.

21
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:14,910
You see that?

22
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:16,380
Even Chuck can hold it.

23
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:18,300
Aren't you guys embarrassed?

24
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:26,940
Don't move!

25
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:29,340
Why are you running?

26
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:36,540
Chuck...

27
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,940
You dare?

28
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:40,860
Coach, have mercy on me!

29
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:46,140
Your punishment is 100 Yo-Yo Throw drills!

30
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:47,580
Coach, that's way too many!

31
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,020
50 then!

32
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:50,430
Still too many!

33
00:02:50,440 --> 00:02:51,390
200!

34
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:52,380
Coach!

35
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:54,780
I'll go do them right now!

36
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:05,340
Keep training!

37
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:16,380
Hey! Where's my chicken leg? Why is it gone?

38
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,780
Chef! Chef!

39
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:23,100
Chef, look at this fish!

40
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,940
What the... who did this?

41
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:29,340
Focus on the fluidity of the motion.

42
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:31,260
Remember, during Competition,

43
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:34,140
your fluidity after a move is also scored.

44
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:37,020
Coach Tony! Coach Tony!

45
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:39,900
Coach Tony!

46
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:43,260
We've got a big problem!

47
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:46,620
My Chef wants to see you.

48
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:47,580
Big problem?

49
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:06,780
No way. Could it have been...

50
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:12,540
A small animal? Like a cat or a dog?

51
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:14,460
No way.

52
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:16,380
All the Evidence suggests...

53
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:18,300
that this was done by a person.

54
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:19,740
And an experienced one at that.

55
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:23,580
Why do you say that?

56
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,980
Take a look for yourself.

57
00:04:26,440 --> 00:04:27,900
This guy only eats the chicken legs.

58
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,780
And with the fish, he only ate the bottom half.

59
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:33,430
Everything else was left perfectly neat.

60
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:36,540
On the surface, you can't even tell anything's missing.

61
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:38,940
This guy's a real Pro.

62
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:42,300
I mean, a cat or a dog couldn't pull this off, right?

63
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:45,660
And another thing! Our tomatoes in the kitchen...

64
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:49,020
cucumbers, and fried peanuts are all missing too!

65
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:53,340
Coach Tony, right now, in the entire Falcon Camp...

66
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:54,780
your Training Camp Squad is the only one here.

67
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:02,430
This is bad. This is really bad.

68
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:04,380
I'm so sorry, Chefs.

69
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:12,400
Who was responsible for this?

70
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:15,700
You'd better step forward and confess right now.

71
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,980
I'm sorry, chefs. I'm really sorry.

72
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:30,300
I'll get to the bottom of this.
I'll Investigate this thoroughly.

73
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:44,700
Coach Tony.

74
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:46,620
You definitely think

75
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,540
it was me who stole the food,

76
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,420
but you just don't have any proof, right?

77
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:56,700
Until the truth comes out,

78
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:58,790
anyone could've done it.

79
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:02,460
Stop being so polite! I can already feel it.

80
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,380
You suspect me.

81
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:09,660
I never said that.

82
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:13,500
I am pursuing the highest realm of Yo-Yo mastery.

83
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:16,380
It requires a mind and body free of distractions.

84
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:20,700
Right now, only the air, the scents,

85
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:23,580
the light, the shadows, the dark clouds...

86
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:25,500
are what truly matter to me.

87
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:27,420
You don't actually think

88
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:29,340
I would steal a chicken leg

89
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:31,260
and ruin my own training, do you?

90
00:06:57,160 --> 00:07:01,020
Who did this? It's so embarrassing!

91
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:06,780
Coach Tony.

92
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:07,710
Manager Ma.

93
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:08,700
I was just about to look for you.

94
00:07:09,060 --> 00:07:11,100
Manager Ma, I'm really sorry about this.

95
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:13,980
I still haven't gotten to the bottom
of that whole kitchen incident.

96
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:16,860
Don't worry about that. They're just kids.

97
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:22,620
Coach Tony, there's something I wanted to ask you.

98
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:24,510
Are you guys here for a 1-Month Training Camp...

99
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:25,500
or a 2-Week Training Camp?

100
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:26,940
1 month, definitely.

101
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:28,830
I mean, that's what we agreed on, right?

102
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:32,700
Yeah, but the deposit you guys
paid was only enough for 2 weeks.

103
00:07:34,600 --> 00:07:36,540
Yeah... about that.

104
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:37,980
I'll figure something else out.

105
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:40,380
Coach Tony.

106
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:42,300
We're a Business operation here, you know.

107
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:44,700
I have a lot of people waiting for their pay checks.

108
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:49,020
So please, don't make this too hard on me.

109
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:52,860
No, I mean, of course not. It won't be.

110
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:57,180
Alright, well, I'll be heading off then.

111
00:07:57,640 --> 00:07:58,140
Okay, take care.

112
00:07:58,760 --> 00:08:00,540
See ya. -See ya.

113
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:22,620
Matthew, keep training hard!

114
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:44,220
Popcorn! Not bad.

115
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:46,140
Of course.

116
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,580
How come you're not in uniform?

117
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:49,980
It's nice to wear my own clothes once in a while.

118
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,830
Plus, I washed my uniform yesterday,
and it's still not dry.

119
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:53,340
Captain.

120
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:57,660
Come on, it's just 1 day. Let it slide.

121
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:02,460
Alright, fine. But make sure you wear it tomorrow.

122
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:03,420
Got it, Captain.

123
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:13,950
Popcorn! Aren't you afraid Coach is
gonna yell at you for dressing like that?

124
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:14,940
Stay out of this.

125
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:16,860
The Captain already gave me permission.

126
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:21,180
Coach Tony had to head back to take care of some Business.

127
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:23,910
I'm in full charge of training for the next couple of days.

128
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:25,950
Everyone got that?

129
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:29,310
Who are you looking for?

130
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:33,630
I just need to head upstairs for something.

131
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:35,070
"No Soliciting."

132
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:36,990
Oh, then you've got the wrong idea.

133
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:38,910
I'm not here to sell anything.

134
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:39,870
I'm here to discuss a Sponsorship.

135
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:41,240
What? A Sponsorship?

136
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,050
Yeah.

137
00:09:42,460 --> 00:09:44,230
Then you definitely can't go in.

138
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:45,550
Out! Out you go!

139
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Out!

140
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:01,500
Popcorn!

141
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,870
That outfit looks really good on you today.

142
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:04,860
You've got real star quality.

143
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:08,700
Really? Someone once told me I looked like a Spice Girl.

144
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:10,840
Oh, you're way better than a Spice Girl.

145
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,060
That's what my mom says, too.

146
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:20,220
I heard you were in a commercial for cookies once.

147
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:22,140
I love those cookies!

148
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:23,580
I'll have to look out for it.

149
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:26,430
Okay, sure. Look for this one scene

150
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,350
where a bunch of girls jump up in the air.

151
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,300
The second girl in the back row... that's me!

152
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,180
And your skin is amazing, too.

153
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:34,720
You should be in skincare commercials.

154
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,500
That's what my mom says, too.

155
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:39,420
And your hair.

156
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:40,860
Your hair is so unique.

157
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:42,300
You could shoot a wig commercial.

158
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,000
What?

159
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,660
No, no, no. A shampoo commercial.

160
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:49,500
Meatball!

161
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:55,260
Monica.

162
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:56,700
I borrowed a hat from the dining hall for you.

163
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,070
So you don't get sunburned. Put it on.

164
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:01,500
How can I wear an ugly hat like this?

165
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,830
I'll wear it! I'll wear it!

166
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,780
Get out of here. This doesn't concern you.

167
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:11,550
Yesterday, I went and bought all the snacks

168
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:12,540
you wanted to eat.

169
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:14,910
Well, hurry up and give them to me then!

170
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:15,900
You want them right now?

171
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Of course!

172
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:19,470
If I don't eat them during break, when am I supposed to?

173
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Chuck!

174
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:23,550
go back to the dorm for me

175
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:25,020
and grab that bag of snacks off the table.

176
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:28,860
Where can you even buy snacks around here?

177
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:31,260
Shoo, shoo. Don't ask questions you shouldn't ask.

178
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:32,660
Hurry up! Go and come right back.

179
00:11:36,520 --> 00:11:38,460
Got a crush and forgot your friends, huh?

180
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:41,820
Man, what a hopeless guy.

181
00:11:43,720 --> 00:11:46,240
Everyone, let's do "The Sleeper" 1 more time!
Keep it synchronized!

182
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:49,500
Captain, can we switch to a different drill?

183
00:11:49,960 --> 00:11:51,900
We've done this one a million times already.

184
00:11:52,640 --> 00:11:53,340
Don't be so impatient.

185
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,740
Even though this is the most basic skill,

186
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:57,660
it's the best way to control

187
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:59,580
the spin time of your Yo-Yo.

188
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:02,460
And it's the most essential Secret
of every single Top-Tier Player.

189
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:05,340
Alright. Listen for my Command. This is the last time.

190
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:08,700
1, 2, 3... go!

191
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:19,500
Stop!

192
00:12:25,460 --> 00:12:26,060
Leo!

193
00:12:27,400 --> 00:12:28,380
You were too slow on the release.

194
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:30,780
Later, you'll do 50 reps as punishment.

195
00:12:31,520 --> 00:12:32,700
No problem.

196
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,140
He's clearly just picking on him.

197
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:39,420
Next up! "Forward Pass"!

198
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:42,780
1, 2, 3... go!

199
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:51,420
Leo, you were too fast this time.

200
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:54,300
You can do 100 reps later as punishment.

201
00:12:57,060 --> 00:12:57,660
Fine.

202
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Mark!

203
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:01,980
You're being totally unfair!

204
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:03,900
Mini, stay out of this.

205
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:07,740
It's fine.

206
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:11,580
Next! "Around the world!"

207
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:12,540
Captain.

208
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:16,350
Everyone knows I'm the best at string tricks.

209
00:13:16,360 --> 00:13:17,340
Can I just skip this one?

210
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:20,700
Fine.

211
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:23,580
Teddy is the best at string tricks.

212
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:25,500
He can skip this one.

213
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:27,420
Just come back and work on the next drill later.

214
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:35,580
Captain, my looping tricks are the best too.

215
00:13:35,740 --> 00:13:37,020
So when we get to "Lightning Fast,"

216
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,940
can I take a break, too?

217
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:40,860
No way. Who said yours is the best?

218
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:43,260
Keep practicing.

219
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:47,580
Miss, I really think

220
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:49,950
you should go talk to your Manager again, alright?

221
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:52,380
Our Jianghai Team is going to
be the future Championship Team.

222
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:54,780
If your Company Sponsors our Team,

223
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,220
it would be

224
00:13:56,680 --> 00:13:58,140
a huge promotional boost for you guys.

225
00:13:58,600 --> 00:13:59,550
I'm sorry, sir.

226
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:00,540
Our Manager already gave us strict instructions.

227
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:01,980
Our products are already

228
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:03,900
selling extremely well in the market.

229
00:14:04,060 --> 00:14:05,820
We really don't need your kind of publicity.

230
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,260
You should probably just head back now.

231
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:08,220
Right?

232
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:09,180
Goodbye, sir.

233
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,580
Miss, I feel like...

234
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:12,990
you guys should try to see the bigger picture here,

235
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:13,860
you know?

236
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:15,420
Why won't you just leave?

237
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:16,860
I'm gonna call security!

238
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:19,740
Okay, okay! I'm going, I'm going!

239
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:20,700
I just think

240
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:21,660
that with you guys...

241
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:24,060
I just think it's a real shame.

242
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:37,500
That guy's really training hard.

243
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:40,860
And Mini... I can't believe she actually stood up for him.

244
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:43,740
Well, he did come back from living abroad.

245
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:45,660
Don't be ridiculous.

246
00:14:47,080 --> 00:14:49,020
Looks like we seriously overestimated him.

247
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:51,420
If he were really that good,

248
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:53,820
he would've reacted to me provoking him so obviously.

249
00:14:54,760 --> 00:14:57,180
If he's not just an idiot, then he must be scared.

250
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,540
I don't think it's that simple.

251
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:04,860
Guys who hide their true strength
are usually the most dangerous kind.

252
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,740
So what do we do now?

253
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:09,660
I'll figure out how to handle him.

254
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,140
That's 68 times now.

255
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:24,540
You got this!

256
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:30,780
Leo! Since you've got someone keeping you company,
how about you go for another 100 reps?

257
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,700
Teddy, don't be such a jerk.

258
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:36,060
Since when do you get to talk?

259
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:37,980
I can say whatever I want.

260
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:40,860
I can't believe you had the nerve to
say your looping tricks are the best.

261
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:42,780
You're totally overestimating yourself.

262
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:43,710
Didn't you also say

263
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:45,660
that your string tricks were the best?

264
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:47,580
Aren't you overestimating yourself, too?

265
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:49,980
Sounds like you've got a problem with me.

266
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:51,900
We'll let the facts do the talking.

267
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:55,230
Fine. That's exactly what I wanted to hear.

268
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:56,700
You pick the time and place.

269
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:58,110
Let's do it right here.

270
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:59,100
Bring it on.

271
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:01,950
But if you lose, you have to accept the punishment.

272
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:02,940
Whatever.

273
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:04,860
Mickey, don't do anything crazy for my sake.

274
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:07,740
I've been wanting to teach him a lesson for a while anyway.

275
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:31,260
Hmph. You asked for this, you little squirt.

276
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:34,620
I'm definitely gonna teach him a lesson.

277
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:48,000
[Name: Teddy | Team: Jianghai]
[Yo-Yo: Vortex | Special Move: Centrifugal Vortex]

278
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:54,500
"Ferris Flying Saucer!"

279
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:57,860
"Centrifugal Vortex!"

280
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:31,260
You lost. Accept your punishment.

281
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:34,620
You really like doing "Lightning Fast," don't you?

282
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:37,980
So I'll make you do "Around the World" instead.

283
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:40,860
What? "Around the World?" That's so lame.

284
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:44,220
Yeah, it's a perfect fit for you.

285
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:47,100
And Remember, it's 200 reps.

286
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:49,470
But...

287
00:18:49,480 --> 00:18:51,900
if you try to slack off, there's nothing I can do about it.

288
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:53,820
Because I'm going back to sleep.

289
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:56,220
I don't have time to count for you.

290
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:58,620
Don't worry. A real man keeps his word.

291
00:18:59,080 --> 00:19:00,540
Only cowards try to weasel out.

292
00:19:03,880 --> 00:19:05,820
You're the man! Alright, let's go.

293
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:09,660
Too easy!

294
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:25,020
If he keeps going at this rate,

295
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:26,940
he won't be done until the crack of dawn.

296
00:19:28,840 --> 00:19:30,750
One day, I'm gonna make him do 200 reps as punishment, too.

297
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:32,220
That'll teach him.

298
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:37,980
Come on. I'll practice with you.

299
00:19:38,920 --> 00:19:41,820
No, it's fine. This is my punishment.
You don't have to join me.

300
00:19:42,280 --> 00:19:43,740
Don't think of it as a punishment.

301
00:19:44,200 --> 00:19:45,150
This is just a fundamental drill.

302
00:19:45,160 --> 00:19:46,620
The more you practice, the better it is for you.

303
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:49,500
Yeah, Mickey. I'll practice with you, too.

304
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:34,140
What a dump.

305
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:37,020
It was so hard to find.

306
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:55,230
Ah! Ouch!

307
00:20:57,160 --> 00:21:00,540
Ouch, ouch, ouch! That hurts so bad!

308
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:03,900
It's all that stupid Director's fault.

309
00:21:04,360 --> 00:21:07,740
Just 1 line of dialogue, and he made me shoot it over 20 times.

310
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:10,620
Making me walk back and forth over and over again! Ouch!

311
00:21:13,660 --> 00:21:15,900
Hey! Driver! Hey!

312
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,000
Wait, wait!

